    what: "#970 (JC-D): an all-iron pickaxe carrying one Forgeweave modifier and a block of foreign state alongside it, pinning that Forgeweave's decode neither drops the foreign half nor lets it displace its own. The foreign block sits under minecraft:custom_data rather than on Apotheosis' real forgeweave:affixes-shaped component types for the same reason m8_socketed.snbt uses minecraft:diamond for its gems: Apotheosis is compileOnly, so its DataComponentTypes are not in any registry a unit test can reach, and ItemStack.CODEC refuses a component type it cannot resolve. Its keys and shape mirror the three components Apotheosis 8.7.0 actually writes (affixes, rarity, affix_name), so what the fixture pins is the rule -- Forgeweave owns its own components and carries everything else through untouched -- rather than Apotheosis' serialization, which is Apotheosis' to change."
